WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:48.155
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:48.425 --> 01:49.265
Hello?

3
02:06.505 --> 02:07.425
What are you doing here?

4
02:07.985 --> 02:09.905
You're so busy you almost forgot your own birthday.

5
02:09.985 --> 02:11.905
I was afraid I wouldn't catch you before midnight,

6
02:11.985 --> 02:12.905
so I came over myself.

7
02:14.065 --> 02:15.265
I'm sorry.

8
02:15.345 --> 02:17.025
I've been swamped all day.

9
02:17.105 --> 02:19.465
I was in the lab all day without my phone.

10
02:20.545 --> 02:22.105
We still have time. Get in the car.

11
02:53.425 --> 02:56.025
Happy birthday, Zheng Yu.

12
03:08.865 --> 03:10.065
Make a wish.

13
03:13.265 --> 03:16.385
What's wrong? Don't you have any wishes you want to fulfill?

14
03:19.025 --> 03:20.505
That's not it.

15
03:21.025 --> 03:24.505
It's just that I feel like I can achieve the things I want to do myself.

16
03:24.585 --> 03:27.145
Rather than making a wish,

17
03:27.225 --> 03:28.705
I'd rather believe in myself.

18
03:32.865 --> 03:34.065
Still,

19
03:34.145 --> 03:36.705
candles are meant to be blown out, and cake is meant to be eaten.

20
03:57.585 --> 03:58.425
Oh, right.

21
04:01.785 --> 04:03.545
Here's your gift. Open it.

22
04:13.105 --> 04:14.145
A camera?

23
04:16.305 --> 04:19.944
When we had dinner with Eleonore, I noticed you really liked her camera.

24
04:21.184 --> 04:22.585
Thank you. I like it so much.

25
04:25.425 --> 04:26.865
Now we can use it

26
04:26.945 --> 04:29.465
to capture more moments together.

27
04:32.025 --> 04:34.265
I… I wasn't ready.

28
04:35.265 --> 04:37.025
I think it looks great. Look.

29
04:37.105 --> 04:38.625
What's so great about it?

30
04:38.705 --> 04:40.185
My eyes are closed.

31
04:41.825 --> 04:43.265
That's called being natural.

32
04:43.345 --> 04:45.345
Look at the photos you usually take.

33
04:45.425 --> 04:47.945
Every single one is as stiff as an ID photo.

34
04:49.105 --> 04:50.305
No, they aren't.

35
04:51.625 --> 04:52.865
I'll find one and show you.

36
04:53.705 --> 04:54.865
What are you doing?

37
04:56.305 --> 04:57.185
This one's pretty good.

38
04:57.265 --> 05:00.545
What's good about it? My mouth is wide open!

39
05:00.625 --> 05:02.945
That's called being natural. Look at your usual photos.

40
05:03.025 --> 05:05.385
-You're always so stiff, just like-- -Don't you dare.

41
05:13.065 --> 05:14.345
Give it to me.

42
05:14.425 --> 05:15.705
I think this photo is pretty good.

43
05:15.785 --> 05:18.145
-Give it to me! You made me look bad! -I'll help you take one more.

44
05:18.225 --> 05:19.305
-Let me do it! -One more!

45
05:19.385 --> 05:21.425
-Give it back! -One last shot! I'll take a proper one.

46
05:21.505 --> 05:23.145
-Give it to me! -One last chance!

47
05:34.945 --> 05:35.825
What's wrong?

48
05:37.345 --> 05:38.505
I have a question.

49
05:39.905 --> 05:40.745
Go ahead.

50
05:42.425 --> 05:45.265
You spend all day doing lab work.

51
05:45.345 --> 05:46.665
How do you still have abs?

52
05:52.625 --> 05:53.585
That's your question?

53
05:59.185 --> 06:03.305
When doing lab work, to a certain extent, frequent standing and manual procedures

54
06:03.385 --> 06:06.345
keep your core muscles in a state of static activation.

55
06:08.465 --> 06:11.625
Are you really calling doing lab work

56
06:11.705 --> 06:12.625
a workout?

57
06:13.865 --> 06:15.505
I do other exercises too.

58
06:15.585 --> 06:19.105
After all, research work eventually comes down to physical endurance too.

59
06:19.985 --> 06:21.665
Does that answer satisfy you, Ms. Zheng?

60
06:25.225 --> 06:26.105
Well…

61
06:27.105 --> 06:28.025
Can I touch them?

62
06:31.825 --> 06:33.745
Consider it my birthday perk.

63
06:35.265 --> 06:36.105
Sure.

64
06:43.025 --> 06:44.625
Just to be clear,

65
06:44.705 --> 06:47.905
I'm purely curious.

66
06:48.545 --> 06:50.145
My intentions are completely innocent.

67
06:57.145 --> 06:58.265
Well, mine aren't.

68
07:33.705 --> 07:34.625
Zheng Yu…

69
08:30.425 --> 08:32.425
Why did it suddenly get so cold?

70
08:32.505 --> 08:34.425
Make sure to dress warmly when you go to the lab today.

71
08:36.505 --> 08:39.345
Who told you to lie to Xiaomian last time about it suddenly getting colder?

72
08:39.425 --> 08:41.945
Look at it now. His words actually came true.

73
08:43.024 --> 08:45.665
Wait, are you still holding a grudge?

74
08:47.025 --> 08:49.065
You kept our relationship a secret. Of course I am.

75
08:50.105 --> 08:52.265
Didn't I already make up for it?

76
08:54.425 --> 08:55.265
Eat up.

77
09:07.785 --> 09:10.065
I knew you were acting suspicious lately!

78
09:10.145 --> 09:12.705
Did I pull so many all-nighters in the lab that I'm hallucinating?

79
09:12.785 --> 09:14.825
This has to be an overseas scam targeting me.

80
09:14.905 --> 09:16.905
Congratulations!

81
09:16.985 --> 09:19.225
So this is the new roommate who is a really good person?

82
09:19.305 --> 09:20.745
He looks pretty familiar.

83
09:20.825 --> 09:22.465
I see right through it, but I'm staying quiet.

84
09:22.545 --> 09:24.665
You're already a college student, can't you read the room?

85
09:24.745 --> 09:27.145
Ms. Zheng, I love you!

86
09:27.225 --> 09:28.185
Congratulations!

87
09:28.265 --> 09:30.065
Are my eyes playing tricks on me?

88
09:30.625 --> 09:33.025
I just put on my new prescription glasses.

89
09:33.105 --> 09:34.945
I don't think your eyes are playing tricks on you.

90
09:35.025 --> 09:37.865
Why am I so shy to click on this?

91
09:39.105 --> 09:41.225
I told my parents last night about us being together.

92
09:43.745 --> 09:45.265
You… What did you say?

93
09:46.545 --> 09:48.385
You already posted on Moments, didn't you?

94
09:48.465 --> 09:50.465
So it's only natural that I tell them.

95
09:52.145 --> 09:53.665
What did your parents say?

96
09:55.065 --> 09:56.425
They didn't say much.

97
10:00.585 --> 10:02.385
They just complained that I moved way too slowly.

98
10:02.465 --> 10:06.065
They said if I'd been a bit more proactive back when you were still in Qingyi,

99
10:06.145 --> 10:08.785
they could have found an excuse to invite you over for dinner.

100
10:10.865 --> 10:11.705
They also said

101
10:11.785 --> 10:14.385
I should share your WeChat with them so you can chat sometime.

102
10:15.905 --> 10:17.905
Okay. Go ahead and share it.

103
10:19.185 --> 10:20.345
Wait, no.

104
10:21.225 --> 10:23.305
Shouldn't I reach out to them first?

105
10:23.945 --> 10:26.625
Why don't you share their contacts with me? I'll add them myself.

106
10:26.705 --> 10:29.745
I'll arrange a time with them for a video call.

107
10:31.505 --> 10:32.705
Really?

108
10:41.265 --> 10:44.425
Since that's settled, and they're calling now, why don't we just--

109
10:44.505 --> 10:45.825
Wait!

110
10:47.345 --> 10:48.705
I'm not ready!

111
10:57.705 --> 10:58.985
ALARM

112
10:59.705 --> 11:02.025
Chen Yanzhou! How dare you trick me!

113
11:02.625 --> 11:04.945
-I'll teach you a lesson! -Hey, friendly reminder!

114
11:05.025 --> 11:07.305
If you don't get changed now, you'll be late for class.

115
11:09.065 --> 11:10.785
Well, you'll be late for your work too!

116
11:12.185 --> 11:14.065
Do we really have to destroy each other like this?

117
11:17.025 --> 11:20.545
I'll settle the score with you after class then.

118
11:28.585 --> 11:30.065
I'll get going.

119
11:31.545 --> 11:32.505
Be safe.

120
11:33.705 --> 11:34.585
Bye.

121
12:35.905 --> 12:37.065
I'm back.

122
13:27.425 --> 13:29.385
I wonder if there's a paper titled,

123
13:29.465 --> 13:31.905
"How to Deal With a Girlfriend Who's Too Into Studying."

124
13:31.985 --> 13:33.345
There probably is.

125
13:35.145 --> 13:36.425
Or maybe,

126
13:36.505 --> 13:40.585
"On the Dangers of Having a Girlfriend Who Only Cares About Studying,

127
13:40.665 --> 13:41.825
and How to Deal With Them."

128
13:50.945 --> 13:53.865
Who was it this morning who said she'd settle the score with me after class?

129
13:55.025 --> 13:56.265
And now that I'm back,

130
13:56.345 --> 13:59.465
forget settling scores, you're completely ignoring me.

131
14:01.025 --> 14:03.185
Who begs someone to settle a score with them?

132
14:07.785 --> 14:09.945
The project timeline has been moved up.

133
14:11.425 --> 14:12.305
Moved up?

134
14:14.265 --> 14:16.185
My advisor sent an email about it.

135
14:16.265 --> 14:19.265
So from now on, I might be really busy and won't have much time for you.

136
14:41.825 --> 14:43.145
What are you doing?

137
14:43.745 --> 14:45.185
Who says you won't have time for me?

138
14:45.985 --> 14:47.665
You can keep me company while I study.

139
17:45.425 --> 17:46.385
Why are you rushing over?

140
17:47.705 --> 17:50.425
Don't tell me you knew I'd be working late

141
17:51.585 --> 17:53.105
and came all the way here to pick me up.

142
17:54.225 --> 17:57.345
I just got off work, and I thought I might catch you here.

143
17:58.625 --> 18:00.025
I was worried earlier

144
18:00.105 --> 18:02.585
that I'd be too busy to spend time with you.

145
18:03.225 --> 18:05.025
Looks like I was overthinking it.

146
18:06.025 --> 18:08.265
You seem to be even busier than I am.

147
18:13.785 --> 18:14.625
What's wrong?

148
18:17.985 --> 18:21.065
I had a meeting with my professor today and got totally chewed out.

149
18:21.145 --> 18:24.785
Our whole previous training plan has to be completely scrapped.

150
18:25.305 --> 18:26.785
We might have to start over from scratch.

151
18:26.865 --> 18:29.065
Then what about your presentation next week?

152
18:29.785 --> 18:32.785
Marco said we should just tell them the truth.

153
18:32.865 --> 18:35.625
They're more interested in how we work through the problems.

154
18:36.825 --> 18:37.665
But I…

155
18:37.745 --> 18:40.705
But you still want to deliver solid results.

156
18:45.545 --> 18:46.385
Chen Yanzhou.

157
18:46.465 --> 18:49.945
Do you remember when you took a leave of absence?

158
18:50.025 --> 18:51.345
You took a whole year off,

159
18:51.425 --> 18:53.545
yet you still won the Vitality Award when you came back.

160
18:53.625 --> 18:54.785
And for this internship,

161
18:54.865 --> 18:58.105
so many people applied, but in the end,

162
18:58.185 --> 19:01.305
you were the one who passed the interview and got the spot.

163
19:01.385 --> 19:02.585
This time will be the same.

164
19:04.785 --> 19:06.065
This time is different.

165
19:07.425 --> 19:08.545
How is it different?

166
19:11.265 --> 19:12.425
This time,

167
19:13.185 --> 19:14.505
I'm not alone.

168
19:16.985 --> 19:18.265
That's true.

169
19:21.745 --> 19:23.825
So how are things on your end?

170
19:23.905 --> 19:25.865
I still have a lot to revise.

171
19:26.905 --> 19:28.945
The professor will be back from his business trip soon.

172
19:29.025 --> 19:31.025
Part of me is dreading his return,

173
19:31.105 --> 19:34.265
but I also hope he comes back soon so we can work more efficiently.

174
19:37.145 --> 19:39.305
We really are partners in misery, aren't we?

175
19:40.825 --> 19:42.505
Who's your partner in misery?

176
19:43.945 --> 19:45.585
Then what do you think we are right now?

177
19:47.145 --> 19:48.625
We're

178
19:48.705 --> 19:51.265
two poor souls in a foreign land

179
19:51.345 --> 19:54.905
getting tortured by experiments.

180
19:56.385 --> 19:57.625
In that case,

181
19:57.705 --> 19:59.345
we might as well comfort each other.

182
20:14.825 --> 20:16.305
Come on. Let's go home.

183
21:35.585 --> 21:36.745
What brings you here?

184
21:37.465 --> 21:39.385
You've been at it for so long. You need to take a break.

185
21:40.585 --> 21:42.505
All right. Let's go eat.

186
21:43.065 --> 21:44.345
Actually,

187
21:45.265 --> 21:46.865
I brought you a gift.

188
21:49.185 --> 21:50.425
What is it?

189
21:52.545 --> 21:54.305
Is the professor who yelled at you around today?

190
21:54.385 --> 21:55.705
Where's his office?

191
21:55.785 --> 21:56.985
I'll smash his windows.

192
22:00.825 --> 22:02.945
If the institute kicks me out,

193
22:03.025 --> 22:05.065
I'll have no choice but to stay home and cook for you.

194
22:05.145 --> 22:06.705
You'll definitely get tired of me then.

195
22:08.945 --> 22:10.265
You finally smiled.

196
22:14.785 --> 22:16.105
Don't worry about me.

197
22:17.305 --> 22:19.385
Rest assured, I'll never get tired of you.

198
22:20.545 --> 22:21.385
Really?

199
22:22.425 --> 22:23.625
Even if the project starts over,

200
22:23.705 --> 22:26.705
or if you get kicked out of the lab and have to stay at home,

201
22:26.785 --> 22:27.865
I won't ever get tired of you.

202
22:41.545 --> 22:43.545
Come on. Let's get something to eat.

203
22:46.665 --> 22:47.785
What do you feel like eating?

204
22:48.705 --> 22:52.385
Is there anything that'll give me the strength to face the professor's judgment?

205
22:53.305 --> 22:54.145
Sichuan food?

206
22:54.945 --> 22:55.945
Hot pot?

207
22:56.505 --> 22:57.705
Or…

208
22:59.225 --> 23:00.905
I could pick up a stone for you too.

209
23:00.985 --> 23:02.105
No way!

210
23:02.185 --> 23:05.265
-There's a big one over there! -No, I don't want to get expelled!

211
23:13.745 --> 23:14.745
My class is over.

212
23:14.825 --> 23:15.745
CHEN YANZHOU

213
23:15.825 --> 23:18.105
And I'm about to give my presentation.

214
23:20.305 --> 23:21.265
Good luck.

215
23:21.345 --> 23:22.385
You got this!

216
24:29.865 --> 24:31.905
Today's progress presentation is over.

217
24:31.985 --> 24:33.585
Marco said we should go out for a big meal.

218
24:33.665 --> 24:34.785
I'm joining them,

219
24:34.865 --> 24:35.945
so I'll be home a little late.

220
24:36.825 --> 24:37.745
Okay.

221
25:56.305 --> 25:58.945
Didn't you say you were going to a party?

222
26:00.625 --> 26:01.785
They rescheduled.

223
26:02.625 --> 26:04.505
Tomorrow, I'll still come pick you up here.

224
26:06.225 --> 26:08.465
You don't have to. You're busy too.

225
26:09.545 --> 26:11.385
No matter how busy I am, I still get off work.

226
26:12.865 --> 26:16.145
It's only a 15-minute walk from the subway station to home.

227
26:16.225 --> 26:18.825
For those 15 minutes, we don't have to think about anything.

228
26:19.865 --> 26:21.065
Nothing at all?

229
26:25.105 --> 26:26.385
No experiments,

230
26:26.465 --> 26:27.985
no papers,

231
26:28.065 --> 26:29.985
and no thinking about what the professor said.

232
26:30.665 --> 26:31.825
Just look at the trees

233
26:32.585 --> 26:34.105
or the stars in the sky.

234
26:35.065 --> 26:36.185
Or

235
26:36.265 --> 26:37.425
you can just look at me.

236
26:38.505 --> 26:39.865
What's there to look at?

237
26:41.145 --> 26:43.145
-Am I not good-looking? -Narcissist.

238
26:44.625 --> 26:45.625
Chen Yanzhou.

239
26:49.225 --> 26:50.105
Thank you.

240
26:51.145 --> 26:51.985
For what?

241
26:53.305 --> 26:54.665
For coming to pick me up.

242
26:56.745 --> 26:57.625
Feeling better?

243
26:58.705 --> 26:59.745
I'm still upset.

244
27:00.345 --> 27:03.545
But once I get through this, I still have to do what needs to be done.

245
27:08.985 --> 27:11.465
Then just keep going. Don't be afraid of the outcome.

246
27:12.145 --> 27:13.225
Either way,

247
27:14.425 --> 27:16.065
I'll still be here to pick you up tomorrow.

248
27:20.145 --> 27:21.345
Let's go.

249
28:06.745 --> 28:07.625
Zheng Yu.

250
28:15.025 --> 28:16.185
Are you cold?

251
28:18.065 --> 28:19.065
Let's go.

252
28:58.105 --> 29:00.025
What are you doing?

253
29:02.025 --> 29:02.905
Taking a break.

254
29:25.665 --> 29:26.785
What are you doing?

255
29:29.145 --> 29:30.105
Taking a break with you.

256
30:08.505 --> 30:09.905
Tell me.

257
30:09.985 --> 30:12.065
Why is it that even when we're exhausted,

258
30:13.025 --> 30:14.425
we still can't fall asleep?

259
30:15.105 --> 30:17.865
It's because the brain is in a state of hyperarousal.

260
30:18.745 --> 30:20.545
Even when the body is exhausted,

261
30:20.625 --> 30:22.905
the sympathetic nervous system stays active.

262
30:25.425 --> 30:26.665
Are you feeling anxious?

263
30:33.585 --> 30:34.425
Zheng Yu.

264
30:35.705 --> 30:37.185
It's okay to fail in life.

265
30:39.705 --> 30:41.865
I used to have a hard time accepting that,

266
30:41.945 --> 30:45.145
so I pushed myself until I had to take a leave of absence.

267
30:46.105 --> 30:47.425
But even then,

268
30:48.225 --> 30:49.825
the world didn't come crashing down.

269
30:51.225 --> 30:53.505
Your professor let you join the project team

270
30:53.585 --> 30:55.705
because of how well you wrote that previous paper, right?

271
30:59.465 --> 31:02.225
So this is a reward, not a burden.

272
31:03.265 --> 31:04.185
A reward?

273
31:06.305 --> 31:08.105
A reward for all your hard work before.

274
31:08.185 --> 31:10.505
Even if you can't continue with it,

275
31:10.585 --> 31:13.425
you'll just go back to being a student like everyone else.

276
31:14.105 --> 31:15.905
You'll go to class, do your assignments,

277
31:15.985 --> 31:19.105
or apply to join another professor's project team.

278
31:20.425 --> 31:23.065
You haven't fallen off a cliff.

279
31:23.145 --> 31:24.945
You've just returned to solid ground.

280
31:34.505 --> 31:35.705
You're right.

281
31:36.345 --> 31:38.025
I need to loosen up a bit.

282
31:46.705 --> 31:49.505
I suddenly really want to go to the beach and watch the sunrise.

283
31:53.505 --> 31:55.865
Why don't we find some time to go later on?

284
31:58.865 --> 32:00.305
We don't need to find time later.

285
32:02.425 --> 32:03.785
We can go right now.

286
32:05.065 --> 32:06.025
Right now?

287
32:08.225 --> 32:09.825
We can't sleep anyway,

288
32:09.905 --> 32:11.305
so instead of lying here wide awake,

289
32:11.385 --> 32:13.625
we might as well head to the beach now and wait for the sunrise.

290
32:14.745 --> 32:16.265
If we leave right now,

291
32:16.345 --> 32:18.145
we'll get to the beach just in time.

292
32:18.225 --> 32:19.225
Really?

293
32:19.945 --> 32:21.065
Let's go.

294
32:21.585 --> 32:23.425
Then I'd better get ready!

295
32:23.505 --> 32:26.025
Should we bring the camera?

296
32:26.105 --> 32:27.665
And what about the picnic mat?

297
32:27.745 --> 32:28.785
Where did we put it?

298
32:29.465 --> 32:31.945
Under the left cabinet in the storage room, second drawer down.

299
32:39.945 --> 32:43.025
Do you remember the last time we saw the sea together?

300
32:44.025 --> 32:44.905
Qingshan Island.

301
32:47.185 --> 32:50.265
Come to think of it, that legend you told me back then

302
32:50.345 --> 32:51.585
was pretty accurate.

303
32:53.305 --> 32:55.865
When two people climb up here together,

304
32:55.945 --> 32:59.905
the direction of travel of the first ship they see between the lighthouses

305
33:00.665 --> 33:04.425
is where the two will travel to together in the future.

306
33:05.705 --> 33:07.665
Thinking back, that legend really came true.

307
33:09.025 --> 33:10.305
Once we graduate and go home,

308
33:10.385 --> 33:12.665
we should send the Tourism Bureau a commendation letter.

309
33:19.185 --> 33:20.465
What are you thinking about?

310
33:22.265 --> 33:23.985
I was thinking,

311
33:24.065 --> 33:26.465
maybe I've been too cautious all this time.

312
33:26.985 --> 33:31.185
I always thought falling for someone meant giving yourself another weakness.

313
33:31.985 --> 33:33.265
But now…

314
33:34.625 --> 33:35.785
How should I put it?

315
33:35.865 --> 33:40.465
It's like my heart feels more grounded, and I've grown stronger.

316
33:42.465 --> 33:45.345
Carrying things together is so much lighter

317
33:46.025 --> 33:47.545
than toughing it out alone.

318
33:49.705 --> 33:52.945
So from now on, the good and the bad, I'll share everything with you.

319
33:54.025 --> 33:54.905
Me too.

320
33:56.265 --> 33:57.865
Don't keep it all to yourself.

321
33:58.385 --> 33:59.425
You neither.

322
34:30.705 --> 34:33.344
I thought you two would go on a trip once your project wrapped up,

323
34:33.425 --> 34:35.505
but then he ended up going on a business trip instead?

324
34:37.065 --> 34:39.585
The institute sent him out of town. He didn't really have a choice.

325
34:39.665 --> 34:42.945
Besides, doesn't this just prove that his project is going really smoothly?

326
34:43.025 --> 34:43.905
Isn't that a good thing?

327
34:43.985 --> 34:45.985
But you haven't seen each other in half a month!

328
34:46.065 --> 34:47.545
How can you stay so composed?

329
34:48.865 --> 34:51.264
I'm not the type of person

330
34:51.344 --> 34:53.865
who starts crying after being apart for a few days,

331
34:53.945 --> 34:56.344
clinging to her phone and waiting for the other person to reply.

332
34:56.425 --> 34:58.225
That would be so immature.

333
34:59.665 --> 35:01.585
Keep denying it.

334
35:06.025 --> 35:08.825
CHEN YANZHOU, HAVE YOU EATEN?

335
35:25.745 --> 35:27.065
What took you so long to answer?

336
35:28.745 --> 35:30.745
I was studying just now and didn't hear it.

337
35:31.785 --> 35:33.265
How's the studying going?

338
35:34.425 --> 35:35.545
Pretty good.

339
35:35.625 --> 35:37.265
Why is your hair messy?

340
35:39.025 --> 35:40.185
Not that side.

341
35:40.265 --> 35:41.705
The hair on your left is sticking up.

342
35:43.665 --> 35:45.745
No, not there. The bit in front.

343
35:50.425 --> 35:51.465
I'm not sure that's helping.

344
35:56.185 --> 35:57.305
It's all your fault.

345
35:57.385 --> 35:58.905
You were silent all day,

346
35:58.985 --> 36:01.145
and now you show up bossing me around.

347
36:01.225 --> 36:02.625
It's not like you can fix it for me.

348
36:03.585 --> 36:06.185
I was in meetings all day today, and our phones were collected.

349
36:06.265 --> 36:07.185
I just got my phone back

350
36:07.265 --> 36:09.065
and haven't even had time to eat yet.

351
36:11.385 --> 36:12.825
That sounds so exhausting.

352
36:12.905 --> 36:14.345
When will it finally be over?

353
36:14.425 --> 36:15.905
Next week.

354
36:15.985 --> 36:17.065
It might even end early.

355
36:17.665 --> 36:18.505
Really?

356
36:19.865 --> 36:21.905
So just hang in there for a few more days.

357
36:21.985 --> 36:24.185
After that, no more sitting alone staring at a phone anymore.

358
36:26.105 --> 36:28.585
Who's been sitting around staring at their phone?

359
36:31.905 --> 36:33.825
I have.

360
36:36.305 --> 36:38.665
Okay, you should go eat now.

361
36:42.545 --> 36:44.585
I'm going to hang up then.

362
36:45.265 --> 36:46.105
Okay.

363
36:48.945 --> 36:49.865
Bye.

364
37:51.825 --> 37:52.865
CHEN YANZHOU

365
37:52.945 --> 37:55.105
The first phase of the report is finally over.

366
37:55.185 --> 37:56.665
Walking down the street now,

367
37:56.745 --> 37:58.185
everything looks so much brighter.

368
38:08.865 --> 38:11.025
The cherry blossoms in Berlin are blooming.

369
38:23.305 --> 38:24.225
XU FANGLI

370
38:24.305 --> 38:25.825
Since you helped me buy all that stuff,

371
38:25.905 --> 38:26.945
I'll teach you a trick.

372
38:27.025 --> 38:28.905
HIGH-LEVEL CUTENESS AUTHENTIC AND ENDEARING

373
38:28.985 --> 38:31.065
Next time you video call Chen Yanzhou,

374
38:31.145 --> 38:35.105
use this trick to revive the spark that cooled off this past month.

375
38:36.785 --> 38:37.785
That's silly.

376
38:39.225 --> 38:43.105
When it comes to relationships, just missing each other isn't enough.

377
38:43.185 --> 38:46.265
When you don't see each other for a month, it's easy to start feeling distant.

378
38:46.345 --> 38:49.345
The way to bridge the distance is to express your feelings.

379
38:49.425 --> 38:52.985
Do you get it? Just try, you've got nothing to lose.

380
38:53.065 --> 38:54.865
If it doesn't work, you can come back and yell at me.

381
38:54.945 --> 38:56.985
Why aren't you replying?

382
38:57.065 --> 38:58.385
Don't you trust me?

383
38:58.465 --> 39:00.585
I do, I do! You're the expert!

384
39:18.705 --> 39:20.625
Yanzhou, happy birthday.

385
39:20.705 --> 39:22.825
Are you spending your birthday with Xiaozheng?

386
39:22.905 --> 39:25.745
I'm away on a business trip, and she's in Berlin.

387
39:25.825 --> 39:26.905
Well, get back to work.

388
39:26.985 --> 39:28.905
Treat yourself to a nice meal afterward.

389
39:53.825 --> 39:56.105
No way. Are you completely stunned?

390
39:56.865 --> 39:58.945
Or did I show up at a bad time?

391
40:05.625 --> 40:06.745
The cake's getting squashed!

392
40:07.545 --> 40:08.545
Who cares if it's squashed?

393
40:09.545 --> 40:10.825
I'm about to get squashed too!

394
40:16.145 --> 40:16.985
What are you doing?

395
40:18.345 --> 40:21.025
Didn't you say you were getting squashed? I'm trying to put you back in shape.

396
40:24.345 --> 40:27.865
So where are we going to eat the cake?

397
40:44.425 --> 40:45.545
Was the trip tiring?

398
40:45.625 --> 40:48.385
Didn't I tell you I'd be wrapping things up here soon?

399
40:48.465 --> 40:49.545
Did you forget?

400
40:49.625 --> 40:51.465
I got your birthday wrong before,

401
40:51.545 --> 40:53.825
and you said you'd make me pay for it with interest.

402
40:53.905 --> 40:56.625
Then we ended up in different countries, so I couldn't celebrate with you.

403
40:56.705 --> 41:00.105
I couldn't let your birthday pass again, or you might really hold a grudge.

404
41:00.185 --> 41:01.745
So I'm here to pay my debt.

405
41:02.945 --> 41:04.145
How did you find me?

406
41:05.105 --> 41:08.985
I saw the hotel photos you posted, so I thought I'd take a chance.

407
41:12.945 --> 41:14.065
What's wrong?

408
41:14.145 --> 41:17.265
If I'd guessed wrong, I'd just think of it as taking a casual city walk.

409
41:17.345 --> 41:18.945
If I guessed right…

410
41:21.585 --> 41:23.945
Happy birthday, Chen Yanzhou.

411
41:24.505 --> 41:25.705
Make a wish.

412
41:27.905 --> 41:28.745
You…

413
41:28.825 --> 41:30.265
I don't need to make a wish.

414
41:31.625 --> 41:33.105
It's already come true.

415
41:35.105 --> 41:37.945
So over these past two years, besides the principal debt,

416
41:38.025 --> 41:39.545
shouldn't there be interest too?

417
41:39.625 --> 41:40.465
What is the interest?

418
41:45.745 --> 41:46.905
Take a guess.

419
41:56.585 --> 41:57.745
What are you doing?

420
41:58.385 --> 41:59.705
Collecting the interest.

421
42:00.585 --> 42:03.825
I was talking about what's inside my bag. I meant for you to get it yourself.

422
42:07.025 --> 42:08.985
Looks like I misunderstood then.

423
42:10.625 --> 42:12.345
You definitely did that on purpose.

424
42:16.705 --> 42:17.905
A tie?

425
42:31.665 --> 42:32.825
Why are you smiling?

426
42:34.265 --> 42:35.105
No reason.

427
42:36.545 --> 42:37.425
I really like it.

428
42:41.465 --> 42:43.905
You're putting it on right now? Why are you in such a rush?

429
42:46.145 --> 42:46.985
Fair point.

430
42:47.705 --> 42:50.425
I'll keep it safe for now and wear it when an important occasion comes up.

431
43:10.825 --> 43:13.265
I was on a video call with Ms. Yang a few days ago.

432
43:13.345 --> 43:14.505
She knew it was your birthday,

433
43:14.585 --> 43:16.905
so she asked me to wish you a happy birthday.

434
43:16.985 --> 43:17.985
You probably haven't heard,

435
43:18.065 --> 43:20.665
but Ms. Yang moved her mom to a hospital in another city.

436
43:20.745 --> 43:24.025
They built a new care center there

437
43:24.105 --> 43:26.905
specializing in long-term care for patients in vegetative states.

438
43:26.985 --> 43:29.025
That should take a bit of pressure off her as a caregiver.

439
43:30.705 --> 43:32.785
She's still running her livestream like before.

440
43:33.505 --> 43:34.785
It went viral a while back,

441
43:34.865 --> 43:36.825
so a lot of people started following her,

442
43:36.905 --> 43:38.585
sending her encouragement and support.

443
43:38.665 --> 43:41.745
But some people have been nasty too. I've already reported several accounts.

444
43:41.825 --> 43:42.665
Oh, right.

445
43:42.745 --> 43:46.665
Do you remember that convenience store I used to work part-time at?

446
43:46.745 --> 43:52.105
My old boss rented two more storefronts and is hiring managers for them.

447
43:52.185 --> 43:56.385
A few days ago, he posted that he wanted to take his son out to play,

448
43:56.465 --> 43:57.905
and asked for recommendations.

449
43:57.985 --> 43:59.465
I even left him a comment.

450
44:03.425 --> 44:06.385
Chen Yanzhou, why are you so quiet?

451
44:06.465 --> 44:09.425
I just feel like you're like a piggy bank,

452
44:09.505 --> 44:11.745
clattering and spilling out coins right in front of me.

453
44:11.825 --> 44:15.185
Chen Yanzhou! If you think I talk too much, just say so!

454
44:15.265 --> 44:16.625
I never said that!

455
44:18.705 --> 44:21.305
Having you here today makes me really happy.

456
44:22.545 --> 44:23.745
Where do you plan to go tomorrow?

457
44:24.505 --> 44:25.945
I haven't thought about it yet.

458
44:28.745 --> 44:31.665
-I'll take you out tomorrow afternoon. -Do you have time?

459
44:32.665 --> 44:34.265
I've been working overtime for a whole month.

460
44:34.345 --> 44:36.225
Taking half a day off shouldn't be an issue, right?

461
44:38.305 --> 44:39.425
Let's go.

462
44:40.265 --> 44:42.225
I just so happen to have read up on a lot of places.

463
44:42.305 --> 44:43.825
We can go together.

464
44:43.905 --> 44:46.385
Charles Bridge is really famous. We can visit it tomorrow too.

465
48:23.025 --> 48:28.025
Subtitle translation by: Cempaka Malinja
